  "intro": {
    "en": "We're taking a look in the back garden. Make a coffee, sit by the window and look outside. There's a good chance that within ten minutes you'll see at least three of the five birds in this lesson. They live all over Britain, all year round, and nearly all of them visit gardens.\n\nIn this lesson you learn to recognise five birds. For each bird you get three things to look for. Words in bold are parts of a bird; you'll find what they mean right there on the card. For the Blackbird and the House Sparrow we only look at the male; the females look very different and get their own lesson in week 5.\n\nAt the end of the lesson there's a short quiz of eight questions."
  },
  "words": [
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "crown"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The top of the head."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "cheek"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The side of the face, below the eye."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "bib"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "A dark patch on the throat."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "breast"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The front, between throat and belly."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "eye-ring"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "A ring of bare skin or feathers around the eye."
      }
    }
  ],
